Power-on-reset detector: divider, RC delay and a comparator with hysteresis (behavioural, self-made)
* The supply is a piecewise-linear source with an optional sinusoidal ripple in series.
Vsup vraw 0 PWL(@PWL@)
Vrip vdd vraw SIN(0 @RIPPLE@ @RIPPLE_HZ@)
R1 vdd vdiv @R1@
R2 vdiv 0 @R2@
C1 vdiv 0 @C1@ ic=0
* Ideal reference and finite gain. The filtered output feeds back to move the threshold.
Bcmp cmp 0 V = 0.5*(1+tanh(@GAIN@*(v(vdiv)-@VTH@+@HYS@*(v(det)-0.5))))
Rout cmp det @ROUT@
Cout det 0 @COUT@ ic=0
.options reltol=@RELTOL@ abstol=1e-12 vntol=1e-7 method=@METHOD@ maxord=2
.save v(vdd) v(vdiv) v(det)
.end
